      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Personally, I have glasses on my avatar, that when pulled away from my face I'd like to become visible so I can see them when other people \"try them on\". I tried to accomplish this with Poiyomi's Depth FX feature, but that had a couple issues and broke with other cameras active.\n\n(Not the point here, though I wonder if it's a VRC or Poiyomi-related bug?)\n\nI moved to using the Dissolve effect with a local proximity contact, which looks and behaves exactly as I want it to, however they dissolve away while worn in all IsLocal==True clones, as other than using that for remote users and the mentioned VRLabs method for local mirrors, I don't know if I can reliably detect not being in first person. \n\n(By the way, is the avatar in handheld/world cameras treated the same as the mirror clone?)\n\nThis IsFirstPerson parameter would allow me to have the dissolve effect on by default (hiding the glasses), then animate it off for any instance of the avatar with IsFirstPerson==False. (or the other way round)",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-11-15T08:19:45.438Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "In the release note of the OpenBeta 1381, VRChat team suggests using VRLabs's way to detect local mirror. However I think that's bad for several reasons\n\n- I think such a very general purpose parameter should be exist as a built-in parameter for performance.\n\n- The VRCLab's way to detect local mirror requires dead-end. According to the Creator docs, we should not use dead end but such a trick needs.\n\n- VRChat doesn't describe initialization timing of mirror clone avatar is few tick later than first person in any documentation.\n\n- It's not bool so it should use more performance cost.\n\nSo, I request VRChat to have some `IsFirstPerson`.\n\nI considered `IsMirror`, which is suggested on some other OpenBeta cannys, but `IsMirror` is confusing that the value is not true for remote in-mirror avatars. So, I choose `IsFirstPerson` instead of `IsMirror`. \n\nIn addition, I think many want to hide something only for first-person but show for remote and mirror clone (in-camera and in-mirror). So, If we have `IsFirstPerson`, we can have simpler state machine transition.\n\nIf we have `IsMirror`, we have to hide if `IsMirror` = false OR `IsLocal` = false, which is a little complex.",
